{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWmwvnaaxAghQAMiwXwyid","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-Aikxx7/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41a2da80-528b-45fd-8c5c-d394200650f8","uuid":"eda25efc-7422-41b4-a211-09a71be7667c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:42:31.038Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-Aikxx7/README.md","oldString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. The first holds the\nstatic coaching rules; the second holds the per-athlete context (date, profile,\nzones, goal, facts). A `save_fact` write changes only the second block, so the\nrules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute\nwindow read from cache.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":5,"newStart":12,"newLines":8,"lines":[" messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`)."," Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+prompt is two text blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. The first holds the","+static coaching rules; the second holds the per-athlete context (date, profile,","+zones, goal, facts). A `save_fact` write changes only the second block, so the","+rules stay cached. Tool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute","+window read from cache."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UWmwvnaaxAghQAMiwXwyid","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
