{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3tyCiaDHnvg8bZRzs2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`save_fact` writes no longer evict the static instructions. The fix is in `bot.py`, but I could not confirm it against the live API, and it may do nothing for core-only messages (details below).\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two text blocks, each with an ephemeral `cache_control`. The first is the static `INSTRUCTIONS` constant. The second is the per-athlete context (date, profile, zones, goal, facts). A `save_fact` now changes only the second block.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph describes the two blocks.\n- `ANSWER.md`: the cause, the change, verification, the risk, and which parts of the colleague's note applied.\n\n**Verification**\n\nI ran a local round trip with a fake LLM and the save patched out, so no API calls were made and neither `data/athletes.json` nor `logs/usage.jsonl` was written. The static block was identical before and after a `save_fact`, the tail changed and contained the new fact, and the tools array was unchanged within the loop.\n\n**Main risk**\n\nSonnet caches only prefixes of at least 1024 tokens (I believe this is the minimum for `claude-sonnet-4-5`; check the current docs). By my estimate, tools plus instructions on core-only messages come to about 850 tokens. If that's right, the first marker won't cache on those messages, and a `save_fact` still evicts the whole prompt. Messages with `plan` or `race` keywords add tool schemas and may clear the minimum. To confirm, send two messages, then a `save_fact` message, then a third, and check `logs/usage.jsonl`. The round after the save should show `cache_read` covering the instructions and `cache_creation` near the tail size (roughly 200–250 tokens), not ~1000+. If it doesn't, the static block needs more real content. I did not pad it.\n\n**Not changed**\n\nKeyword-based tool selection still changes the tools prefix, and that evicts the instructions too on `plan` and `race` messages. Fixing it means always sending all tools, which costs more on the common path, so I left it for you to decide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2224,"cache_read_input_tokens":41916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2224},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41a2da80-528b-45fd-8c5c-d394200650f8","uuid":"b7a59471-fb11-4216-9cb1-2ac4c7b68a05","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:42:46.363Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3txwqzkG4qm88Kv49q"}
